<LegalLayout title="Privacy policy" path="/privacy" description="How the Dawnlight Labs website handles email enquiries, hosting information and cookieless visitor analytics.">
  <p>This policy covers the Dawnlight Labs website. Dawnlight Labs is an independent research laboratory based in India. For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:contact@dawnlightlabs.com">contact@dawnlightlabs.com</a>. Individual products may have their own policies when released.</p>
  <section class="legal-section"><h2>What this website collects</h2><p>You can browse without an account. This website does not accept payments or provide a message submission form. If you email us, we receive your email address, your message and any attachments you choose to send. We use these to respond and manage the conversation. Please send only information needed for your enquiry.</p><p>Our hosting provider, Vercel, processes request information, which may include IP addresses, browser information and technical logs, to deliver and protect the website.</p></section>
  <section class="legal-section"><h2>Visitor analytics</h2><p>We use Vercel Web Analytics on the production website to understand which pages are useful and how visitors reach them. Its reports include page views, referring websites, approximate country, browser and device information. Vercel describes this service as cookieless; it uses a temporary request-derived identifier that is discarded after 24 hours, rather than a persistent identifier that follows you across websites.</p><p>Our integration removes query strings and URL fragments from page addresses before sending analytics events. It does not send email messages or the contents of the project illustrations. We do not add custom interaction tracking, and we skip analytics when your browser sends the Do Not Track setting. Browser extensions may also block it. See <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy">Vercel’s analytics privacy documentation</a> for its processing details.</p></section>
  <section class="legal-section"><h2>Cookies and the illustrations</h2><p>The website code does not set cookies or use local storage for advertising, analytics or preferences. There are no optional cookie categories to accept. Hosting infrastructure may use necessary security mechanisms.</p><p>The project illustrations run in your browser. They do not access your microphone, run shell commands, connect to an AI model or submit the example interactions to Dawnlight. Their state resets when you reload the page. Copying our email address uses your browser’s clipboard feature only when you press the copy button.</p></section>
  <section class="legal-section"><h2>How we use and share information</h2><p>We use information to reply to enquiries, understand aggregate website usage, maintain security and meet applicable obligations. We never sell personal user data. We do not use information you send us for model training without separate, explicit and informed consent.</p><p>Hosting and email providers process information needed to supply their services. These providers may process information outside India. We may also disclose information where required by law or necessary to protect legitimate legal rights. Links to external websites and your email provider are subject to those services’ policies.</p></section>
  <section class="legal-section"><h2>Retention and your choices</h2><p>We keep correspondence for as long as reasonably needed to handle the enquiry and any related obligations. Hosting and analytics records follow the relevant provider’s retention settings and policies. We do not promise a fixed retention period that all of those systems cannot support.</p><p>You can ask us about information you have supplied, request corrections or deletion, or withdraw consent you previously gave. Email <a href="mailto:contact@dawnlightlabs.com">contact@dawnlightlabs.com</a>. We may need to verify your request, and some information may need to be retained for applicable legal or security reasons. Your rights depend on the law that applies to you.</p></section>
  <section class="legal-section"><h2>Changes and contact</h2><p>We will update this page when the website’s data handling changes. The date above identifies the latest version. Read our <a href="/terms">terms and conditions</a> for website use, or <a href="/contact">contact us</a> with a question.</p></section>
</LegalLayout>
